T("Reading","Reading: The new student","Read a story and answer","🎒","",
 ["Some answers are not written down. You have to work them out from the clues.", "Notice comparisons: \"like a fast river\" tells you how the words felt.", "Ask what the characters want and how they change."],
 ["Why did Dmitri understand almost nothing?|He was still learning the language|He was not listening|The room was too noisy|He was asleep", "What does \"rushed past like a fast river\" suggest?|The words were too quick for him to catch|The classroom was flooded|The teacher was shouting|He liked the sound", "How did Dmitri probably feel at the start of lunch?|Lonely|Excited|Angry|Proud", "What did Amara do first?|She sat down beside him|She gave him a book|She told the teacher|She laughed at him", "How did Amara begin to teach him?|By pointing at things and naming them|By writing a letter|By speaking louder|By using a phone", "What does trading \"twelve words and one cookie\" show?|They were becoming friends|They were arguing|They were bored|They were doing a test", "What is the theme of the story?|Kindness can cross a language barrier|School lunches are too short|Apples are healthy|New students should stay quiet"],"","On his first day, Dmitri understood almost nothing. The teacher's words rushed past like a fast river. At lunch he sat alone, turning an apple in his hands. Then a girl named Amara slid her tray beside his. She pointed at the apple, said \"apple,\" and then pointed at herself and said her name. Dmitri smiled and answered with the word in his own language. By the end of lunch they had traded twelve words and one cookie.");
T("Reading","Reading: The northern lights","Read facts and answer","🌌","",
 ["Find the cause and the effect: what happens first, and what does it lead to?", "A phrase after \"also called\" gives another name for the same thing.", "Details such as place names answer where questions."],
 ["What is another name for the northern lights?|Aurora borealis|Milky Way|Solar eclipse|North Star", "Where do the particles that cause the lights come from?|The Sun|The Moon|Volcanoes|The oceans", "What pulls the particles toward the poles?|The Earth's magnetic field|The wind|The Moon's gravity|The clouds", "What makes the light?|Particles crashing into gases, which then glow|Sunlight bouncing off ice|Lightning in clouds|City lights", "Which colours does the text mention?|Green, pink and violet|Red, white and blue|Yellow and orange|Black and grey", "Where in Canada are the lights seen best?|In the far north|In the south near the border|Only in big cities|Only on the coasts", "What kind of night is best for seeing them?|Dark, clear winter nights|Cloudy summer nights|Rainy nights|Nights with a full moon and fog"],"","The northern lights, also called the aurora borealis, are ribbons of green, pink and violet light that dance across the night sky. They begin at the Sun, which sends out a stream of tiny charged particles. When these particles reach the Earth, they are pulled toward the poles by the planet's magnetic field. There they crash into gases high in the air, and the gases glow. The best places to see the lights are far in the north, such as Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut, on dark, clear winter nights.");
T("Spelling","Canadian spelling","Colour, centre, favourite …","🇨🇦","Which is the usual Canadian spelling?",
 ["Canadian spelling often keeps the u in words like colour and neighbour.", "Words like centre and metre end in re.", "Words like travelled double the l."],
 ["|colour|color|culler|colur", "|centre|center|sentre|centar", "|favourite|favorite|favrite|favourit", "|neighbour|neighbor|nieghbor|naybor", "|metre|meter|meeter|metar", "|honour|honor|onour|honer", "|travelled|traveled|travled|travelld", "|cheque|check|chek|cheke", "|theatre|theater|theeter|theatar", "|grey|gray|gra|greay"],"");
T("Words","Words with two meanings","The same word, different jobs","🔀","",
 ["Some words have more than one meaning.", "The rest of the sentence tells you which meaning is used.", "Try each meaning in the sentence."],
 ["The dog began to bark. What does bark mean here?|The sound a dog makes|The skin of a tree", "She peeled the bark off the log. What does bark mean here?|The skin of a tree|The sound a dog makes", "He hit the ball with a bat. What does bat mean here?|A stick used in a game|A flying animal", "A bat flew out of the cave. What does bat mean here?|A flying animal|A stick used in a game", "We sat on the bank of the river. What does bank mean here?|The land beside a river|A place that keeps money", "She put her savings in the bank. What does bank mean here?|A place that keeps money|The land beside a river", "Turn right at the corner. What does right mean here?|A direction|Correct", "Your answer is right. What does right mean here?|Correct|A direction", "The feather is very light. What does light mean here?|Not heavy|Something that helps you see", "Please turn on the light. What does light mean here?|Something that helps you see|Not heavy"],"");

