T("Reading","Reading: The beaver dam","Read the passage, then answer","🦫","Answer from the passage.",
 ["Read the whole passage first.", "Look back at the passage to find the answer. Do not guess from memory.", "For questions about meaning, read the sentences around the word."],
 ["Where did the beavers live?|In a quiet stream|In a big lake|In a forest cave|On a farm", "When did the beavers cut down trees?|Every evening|Every morning|At noon|Only in winter", "What did the beavers use to cut down trees?|Their strong front teeth|Their tails|Their claws|Sharp stones", "What did they pack the branches with?|Mud|Snow|Leaves|Sand", "What grew behind the dam?|A deep pond|A tall tree|A field of grass|A rocky hill", "Where was the door of the lodge?|Under the water|On the roof|On the shore|In a tree", "What was it like inside the lodge?|Dry and safe|Wet and cold|Bright and noisy|Empty and dark", "How did the beavers reach their food in winter?|They swam under the ice|They walked on the ice|They dug through the snow|They flew south", "What is this passage mostly about?|How beavers build a home|How to catch a fish|Why streams freeze|How trees grow", "What does the word lodge mean in this passage?|The beavers' home|A kind of tree|A pile of food|A frozen pond"],"","A family of beavers lived in a quiet stream. Every evening they cut down small trees with their strong front teeth. They dragged the branches into the water and packed them with mud. Soon a dam stretched across the stream, and a deep pond grew behind it. In the middle of the pond the beavers built a lodge with an underwater door. Inside, it stayed dry and safe. When winter came and ice covered the pond, the beavers swam under the ice to reach the food they had stored.");
