T("Reading","Reading: The first snowfall","Read the passage, then answer","❄️","Answer from the passage.",
 ["Read the whole passage first.", "Look back at the passage to find the answer. Do not guess from memory.", "For questions about meaning, read the sentences around the word."],
 ["When did Amir move to Canada?|In August|In November|In January|In June", "Why did Amir gasp when he opened the curtains?|The street was covered in snow|He was late for school|He saw a moose|The window was broken", "Who gave Amir his boots and mittens?|Mrs. Clark|His teacher|His cousin|The two children", "What sound did the snow make under his feet?|It squeaked|It cracked|It splashed|It rang", "What happened to the snowflake on his sleeve?|It melted|It grew bigger|It blew away|It turned to ice", "What were the two children doing?|Rolling a huge ball for a snowman|Throwing snowballs at cars|Shovelling the driveway|Skating on a pond", "What did the children do when they saw Amir?|They waved him over|They ran away|They laughed at him|They ignored him", "What did Amir have by lunchtime?|Cold fingers, a red nose and two new friends|A sore foot|A new sled|A snow day", "How did Amir most likely feel at the end?|Happy|Angry|Bored|Frightened", "What is the main idea of the passage?|A boy enjoys his first snowfall and makes friends|Winter is dangerous|Snowmen are hard to build|Mittens keep hands warm"],"","Amir had moved to Canada in August, so he had never seen snow. One morning in November he opened the curtains and gasped. The whole street was white. He pulled on the boots and mittens his neighbour, Mrs. Clark, had given him and ran outside. The snow squeaked under his feet. He caught a flake on his sleeve and saw its tiny points before it melted. Across the road, two children were rolling a huge ball for a snowman. They waved him over. By lunchtime Amir had cold fingers, a red nose and two new friends.");
