T("Reading","Reading: The science fair","Read the passage, then answer","🔬","Answer from the passage.",
 ["Read the whole passage first.", "Look back at the passage to find the answer. Do not guess from memory.", "For questions about meaning, read the sentences around the word."],
 ["How long did Priya have to finish her project?|Three weeks|Five days|Two weeks|One month", "What happened to her partner, Jonah?|He moved to another school|He got sick|He did a different project|He forgot about the fair", "What question did Priya test?|Do plants grow faster with music?|Do plants need sunlight?|Which bean grows tallest?|Does a radio use much power?", "Why did she put both plants by the same window?|So they would get the same light|Because there was no other space|To hide them from Jonah|So they could hear the radio", "How long did she play the radio each day?|One hour|Five minutes|All day|Three hours", "How much taller was the plant with music?|One centimetre|Ten centimetres|It was shorter|Exactly the same", "What did Priya write about her test?|It was too short to prove anything|It proved music helps plants|It was the best in the class|It was Jonah's idea", "Why did one judge praise her?|She reported what she really found|She won first prize|She had the tallest plant|She worked with a partner", "Which word best describes Priya at the end?|Honest|Lazy|Angry|Careless", "What lesson does the passage suggest?|Starting late makes good results hard, but honesty still matters|Music always helps plants grow|Partners are not needed|Judges only like winners"],"","Priya had three weeks to finish her science fair project, and for the first two she did almost nothing. Then her partner, Jonah, moved to another school. With five days left, she chose a simple question: do plants grow faster with music? She placed two bean plants by the same window and played the radio beside one of them for an hour each day. On the morning of the fair, the plant with music was only one centimetre taller. Priya wrote honestly that her test was too short to prove anything. The judges did not give her first prize, but one of them praised her for reporting what she really found.");
