T("Writing","Using evidence","Quotations, paraphrases and sources","📑","",
 ["Evidence is the proof you give for a point: facts, examples or words from a text.", "A quotation uses the exact words inside quotation marks. A paraphrase puts the idea in your own words.", "Always say where the evidence came from."],
 ["What is evidence in an essay?|Proof that supports your point|Your opening sentence|The title|A list of topics", "What is a quotation?|The exact words from a source, in quotation marks|An idea in your own words|A summary of a book|A made-up example", "What is a paraphrase?|An idea from a source put in your own words|The exact words from a source|A list of sources|A new opinion", "What must you do after quoting a source?|Say where it came from|Change the words|Remove the quotation marks|Nothing", "What is plagiarism?|Using someone's words or ideas as your own|Quoting with a source|Writing a summary|Asking a teacher for help", "Which is the strongest evidence for a claim about a novel?|A line from the novel that shows it|A friend's opinion|A guess|The colour of the cover", "What should follow a piece of evidence?|An explanation of how it supports your point|Another unrelated fact|The conclusion|The title again", "Which source is most reliable for facts about a country's population?|A national statistics agency|An anonymous comment|An advertisement|A joke website", "Why use quotation marks?|To show the words are exactly from the source|To make the sentence longer|To show strong feeling|To end a paragraph", "When is a paraphrase better than a quotation?|When the idea matters more than the exact words|When you want to copy|When you have no source|Never"]);
