T("Words","Idioms and expressions","Sayings that mean something else","💬","What does it mean?",
 ["An idiom is a saying whose meaning is different from its words.", "A piece of cake means something very easy.", "You learn idioms by seeing them used."],
 ["A piece of cake|Something very easy|A small dessert|A hard problem|A birthday gift", "Break the ice|Start a friendly conversation|Smash a frozen pond|End a friendship|Cool a drink", "Under the weather|Feeling sick|Standing in the rain|Very happy|Lost outside", "Hit the books|Study hard|Throw books away|Close the library|Write a novel", "Once in a blue moon|Very rarely|Every night|At midnight|During an eclipse", "Cost an arm and a leg|Be very expensive|Cause an injury|Be very cheap|Take a long time", "Let the cat out of the bag|Reveal a secret|Free a pet|Buy a cat|Lose a bag", "The ball is in your court|It is your turn to decide|You won the game|The game is over|You lost the ball", "Bite off more than you can chew|Take on too much|Eat too quickly|Refuse to help|Talk too loudly", "On the fence|Unable to decide|Very sure|Sitting outside|In trouble", "Burn the midnight oil|Work late into the night|Waste fuel|Cook at night|Sleep early"]);
T("Reading","Reading: The lighthouse keeper","Read the passage, then answer","🗼","Answer from the passage.",
 ["Read the whole passage first.", "Look back at the passage to find the answer. Do not guess from memory.", "For questions about meaning, read the sentences around the word."],
 ["How long had Mr. Doucette kept the lighthouse?|Thirty years|Ninety-two years|Ten years|Three years", "How many steps did the lighthouse have?|Ninety-two|Thirty|One hundred|Fifty", "What did he do each evening?|He polished the lens and lit the lamp|He went fishing|He painted the tower|He rang a bell", "What replaced the lamp?|An automatic light|A larger lamp|A radio tower|A new keeper", "How did the village honour him?|They held a supper|They built a statue|They named a boat after him|They gave him a medal", "What did people see the next evening?|Him walking up the path as usual|The light turned off|A new keeper arriving|Boats lost at sea", "What did he mean by saying he still needs the light?|The lighthouse is still an important part of his life|He cannot see in the dark|He wants his job back for the pay|The automatic light is broken", "When did he go home?|After the first boat rounded the point|At midnight|When the boy left|At sunrise", "Which word best describes Mr. Doucette?|Devoted|Careless|Greedy|Impatient", "What is a theme of this passage?|Work can give a person a sense of purpose|Machines are dangerous|Fishing is hard|Villages are quiet"],"","For thirty years, Mr. Doucette climbed the ninety-two steps of the lighthouse every evening. He polished the great lens, lit the lamp and watched the fishing boats come home. When the government replaced the lamp with an automatic light, he was told he could retire. The village held a supper in his honour. Yet the next evening, people saw him walking up the path as usual. \"The light does not need me,\" he said to a boy who asked, \"but I still need the light.\" He sat on the top step until the first boat rounded the point, then went home.");
