T("Reading","Reading: The council meeting","Read the passage, then answer","🏛","Answer from the passage.",
 ["Read the whole passage first.", "Look back at the passage to find the answer. Do not guess from memory.", "For questions about meaning, read the sentences around the word."],
 ["What was the council about to vote on?|Closing the Elm Street library|Building a new school|Raising bus fares|Opening a park", "What grade was Tessa in?|Grade 9|Grade 6|Grade 12|Grade 7", "What did Tessa hold?|Three pages of signatures|A map of the town|A library book|Her phone", "What detail shows that Tessa was nervous?|Her hands shook|She spoke loudly|She checked her phone|She put down her pen", "What did Tessa choose NOT to argue?|That the building was beautiful or old|That people used it|That the next branch was far|That students needed it", "Which group did she mention?|Newcomers practising English|Tourists visiting the town|Councillors holding meetings|Bus drivers on break", "How far away was the nearest branch?|Two bus rides|Next door|A short walk|In another province", "How did the two councillors react?|One checked his phone and another listened|Both left the room|Both clapped|Both argued with her", "What happened to the vote?|It was delayed by a month|The library was closed|The library was saved for good|Tessa was asked to leave", "What can you infer from the council asking staff to count users?|They wanted evidence before deciding|They had already decided to close it|They did not believe libraries matter|They wanted to hire Tessa"],"","The town council was about to vote on closing the Elm Street library when a Grade 9 student named Tessa asked to speak. Her hands shook as she held three pages of signatures. She did not argue that the building was beautiful or old. Instead, she listed who used it: seniors reading the newspaper, newcomers practising English, and students with no quiet place at home. She pointed out that the nearest branch was two bus rides away. One councillor checked his phone while she talked. Another put down her pen and listened. The vote was delayed by a month, and the council asked staff to count how many people used the library each week.");

