T("Literature","Symbols and motifs","Objects and ideas that carry meaning","🕊","",
 ["A symbol is an object, person or place that stands for a bigger idea: a dove for peace.", "A motif is an image or idea that repeats through a work.", "An allegory is a whole story in which characters and events stand for something else."],
 ["What is a symbol?|Something that stands for a bigger idea|A list of characters|The order of events|A type of rhyme", "What is a motif?|An image or idea that repeats through a work|The main character|The final chapter|A single metaphor", "What is an allegory?|A story in which characters and events stand for something else|A poem with no rhyme|A true life story|A list of symbols", "A dove often symbolizes|peace|war|hunger|speed", "In many stories, a journey symbolizes|personal growth|a holiday|being lost forever|a map", "A storm in a story often symbolizes|conflict or trouble|a wedding|good luck|a new friendship", "Spring often symbolizes|new beginnings|death|old age|danger", "What is an archetype?|A character type found in many stories, such as the hero or the mentor|A new invention|A kind of stanza|A type of narrator", "A story keeps returning to images of locked doors. This is a|motif|plot twist|setting|narrator", "Light and darkness are often used to symbolize|good and evil|rich and poor|young and old|fast and slow"]);
T("Reading","Reading: The night shift","Read the passage, then answer","🌙","Answer from the passage.",
 ["Read the whole passage first.", "Look back at the passage to find the answer. Do not guess from memory.", "For questions about meaning, read the sentences around the word."],
 ["Why did Dev take the job at the bakery?|It paid a dollar more than the grocery store|He loved baking|His mother worked there|It was close to school", "What had Dev not thought about?|The hours|The pay|The distance|The uniform", "What time did he work?|Four in the morning|Four in the afternoon|Midnight|Noon", "How long had Mrs. Okafor owned the bakery?|Twenty years|One month|Seven years|Four years", "How did Mrs. Okafor teach him?|She showed him once, then watched|She gave him a book|She shouted instructions|She sent him to a class", "How many loaves did Dev ruin?|Six|Seven|One|Twenty", "What did Mrs. Okafor do on the seventh loaf?|She nodded|She clapped|She threw it away|She fired him", "What could Dev do by the end of the month?|Tell from the smell when the bread was ready|Run the bakery alone|Bake cakes|Sleep at work", "What does her nod suggest?|She approved of his work|She was falling asleep|She was angry|She wanted him to leave", "What is a theme of this passage?|Skill and pride can come from patient practice|Money is all that matters|School is useless|Bakers work too hard"],"","Dev took the job at the bakery because it paid a dollar more than the grocery store. He had not thought about the hours. At four in the morning the street outside was silent, and the ovens were the only warm thing in the city. Mrs. Okafor, who had owned the bakery for twenty years, did not talk much. She showed him once how to fold the dough, then watched him ruin six loaves without a word. On the seventh, she nodded. By the end of the month Dev could tell from the smell alone when the bread was ready. He was always tired at school, but for the first time he was good at something nobody had taught him in a classroom.");
