T("Media","Reading the media","Audience, purpose and point of view","📺","",
 ["Every media text is made by someone, for an audience, with a purpose.", "The purpose may be to inform, persuade, entertain or sell.", "Ask whose point of view is shown and whose is left out."],
 ["What is a target audience?|The group a media text is made for|The people who made it|The actors in it|The price of it", "What is the main purpose of an advertisement?|To persuade people to buy or do something|To report the news|To tell a true story|To teach grammar", "What is the main purpose of a news report?|To inform|To sell a product|To entertain with jokes|To tell a fairy tale", "What does it mean to ask whose voice is missing?|To notice which groups or views are left out|To check the volume|To find the narrator|To count the speakers", "What is a stereotype?|An oversimplified idea about a group of people|A kind of headline|A sound effect|A camera angle", "What is a headline meant to do?|Grab attention and sum up the story|Give every detail|Name the reporter|List the sources", "A low camera angle looking up at a person makes them seem|powerful|weak|small|funny", "What is sponsored content?|Material paid for by an advertiser|A free public service|A government report|A reader's letter", "Which is an example of loaded language?|The reckless plan|The plan|The new plan|The plan announced on Monday", "How can you check a claim you see online?|Look for the same fact in reliable sources|Count the likes|Trust the first result|Share it and see"]);
T("Reading","Reading: The interview","Read the passage, then answer","💼","Answer from the passage.",
 ["Read the whole passage first.", "Look back at the passage to find the answer. Do not guess from memory.", "For questions about meaning, read the sentences around the word."],
 ["How many questions had Amara prepared for?|Forty|Two hundred|Three|Four", "What was the first question?|Tell me about a time you failed|Why do you want this job?|What are your strengths?|Where do you live?", "What failure did she think of?|Freezing in the debate final|Failing a math test|Losing a race|Missing the interview", "How many people had been watching the debate?|Two hundred|Forty|Three|A dozen", "What did she consider doing instead of telling the truth?|Inventing something smaller|Leaving the room|Blaming her team|Saying she never failed", "What did she ask the coach the following year?|To let her speak first|To leave the team|To change partners|To skip the final", "What did the manager do as she spoke?|He wrote nothing down|He took many notes|He checked his phone|He interrupted her", "What had she done the night after the loss?|Watched the whole recording|Gone to a party|Quit the team|Called the manager", "What does watching the recording suggest about Amara?|She faces her mistakes in order to improve|She likes watching films|She blames others|She gives up easily", "What does the last sentence most likely mean?|She was offered the job|She lost her phone|The manager forgot her|The debate coach called"],"","Amara had prepared answers to forty questions, but not to the first one the manager asked. \"Tell me about a time you failed.\" She thought of the debate final, when she had frozen in front of two hundred people and lost the round for her team. For a moment she considered inventing something smaller. Instead she told the truth, including the part where she had asked the coach to let her speak first the following year. The manager wrote nothing down. He only asked what she had done the night after the loss. \"I watched the recording,\" Amara said, \"all of it.\" Three days later the phone rang.");
