T("Reading","Reading: The last ferry","Read the passage, then answer","⛴","Answer from the passage.",
 ["Read the whole passage first.", "Look back at the passage to find the answer. Do not guess from memory.", "For questions about meaning, read the sentences around the word."],
 ["When did the last ferry leave?|At six|At four|At eleven|At noon", "For how many years had the grandfather refused to leave in October?|Eleven|Four|Forty|Six", "How long had Nadia driven?|Four hours|Forty minutes|Eleven hours|Six hours", "What did Nadia do instead of arguing?|She made tea and asked about the dock|She packed his bags|She called her mother|She left without him", "How long did he talk?|Forty minutes|Four hours|Six minutes|All night", "What did he do when he had finished talking?|He looked at the clock, sighed and found his coat|He went to bed|He refused again|He made more tea", "Why did Nadia's approach work?|Listening let him leave in his own time|She tricked him|She frightened him|She promised him money", "What did he watch from the rail?|The house, until the fog took it|The other passengers|The city lights|The dock he was arriving at", "What does his last remark show?|He wants more time with her on the island|He is angry with her|He plans to sell the house|He dislikes the ferry", "Which word best describes Nadia?|Patient|Impatient|Careless|Stubborn"],"","The last ferry of the season left at six, and Nadia's grandfather refused to be on it. He stood in the kitchen of the island house with his arms folded, as he had every October for eleven years. Nadia had driven four hours to collect him. She did not argue. She made tea, sat down and asked him to tell her again how he had built the dock. He talked for forty minutes. When he had finished, he looked at the clock, sighed and went to find his coat. On the crossing he stood at the rail and watched the house until the fog took it. \"Next year,\" he said, \"you will come in June, and stay.\"");

